type: software
title: "大模型的小练习（一）：Written on the Wall II 猜想 #138 的反例"
version: "1.2.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24538089"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
authors:
  - name: "yutitan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yutitan/wowii-conjecture-138"
url: "https://github.com/yutitan/wowii-conjecture-138"
abstract: >-
  Explicit trees that violate conjecture #138 of Written on the Wall II
  (Graffiti.pc): path(G) >= (2+u(G))*dist_min(M(G^2)).  The smallest
  counterexamples are three trees on 18 vertices; none exists with fewer
  vertices.  Includes a standard-library verification script, an exhaustive
  search over unlabeled trees, and a Lean 4 formalization of one of the
  18-vertex witnesses (one witness only; the three-witness count and the
  exhaustive minimality search are not formalized).
keywords:
  - graph theory
  - path number
  - independent set
  - Graffiti.pc
  - Written on the Wall
  - counterexample
license: MIT
notes: >-
  Series: 大模型的小练习（一） (LLM Exercises I); entry (二) is
  https://github.com/yutitan/langton-ant-three-rows. The title was changed
  from the earlier English title for series numbering; the mathematical
  content is unchanged since v1.1.0.
  Derived with GPT 6.2 Astra (OpenAI Codex, model gpt-6.2-astra): the 21-vertex
  witness T21 was derived at 2026-11-25 13:12:32 UTC in a session directed by
  the author. The three minimal 18-vertex trees were found by exhaustive search
  over all unlabeled trees with 3-18 vertices. The repository was first
  published on 2026-11-25. This is a public record of a personal AI-assisted
  exploration and makes no priority claim. See PROVENANCE.md for the timeline
  and the AI disclosure.
  Archived at Zenodo under DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24538089 (concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24538088).
  A Lean 4 formalization of one 18-vertex witness was added on 2026-11-26 (see
  lean/README.md); it does not cover the three-witness count or the exhaustive
  minimality search.
